# Zoom-Related Code Analysis from Raw Interpreter

## 1. Polygon Vertex Reading with Zoom

The `readVertices` function scales coordinates by zoom:

```c
void Polygon::readVertices(const uint8_t *p, uint16_t zoom) {
	bbw = (*p++) * zoom / 64;
	bbh = (*p++) * zoom / 64;
	numPoints = *p++;
	for (int i = 0; i < numPoints; ++i) {
		Point *pt = &points[i];
		pt->x = (*p++) * zoom / 64;
		pt->y = (*p++) * zoom / 64;
	}
}
```

Bounding box dimensions and all vertex coordinates are multiplied by the zoom factor, then divided by 64.

## 2. Drawing Pipeline with Zoom

The `readAndDrawPolygon` function accepts zoom as a parameter and passes it through the hierarchy:

```c
void Video::readAndDrawPolygon(uint8_t color, uint16_t zoom, 
                                const Point &pt)
```

When vertices are encountered (when `i >= 0xC0`), the zoom value is applied during vertex reading, then `fillPolygon` processes the scaled vertices.

## 3. Hierarchical Polygon Processing

The `readAndDrawPolygonHierarchy` function maintains zoom throughout recursion:

```c
void Video::readAndDrawPolygonHierarchy(uint16_t zoom, const Point &pgc) {
	Point pt(pgc);
	pt.x -= _pData.fetchByte() * zoom / 64;
	pt.y -= _pData.fetchByte() * zoom / 64;
	// ...child polygons processed with same zoom
	readAndDrawPolygon(color, zoom, po);
}
```

Offset calculations also apply the zoom scaling factor.

## 4. Missing Information

The provided code excerpt does not include opcode handlers (`op_selectVideoPage`, `op_fillVideoPage`, etc.) or the video opcode 0x40 extended handler that would show how zoom values are passed from bytecode interpretation to drawing functions.

